1
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:43,020
It'll work out somehow.

2
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without a job, come to me.

3
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,480
I don't have one either, but don't worry.

4
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:11,900
Look, the Akaneru is burning too.

5
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:18,240
It'll work out eventually.

6
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:23,480
You get it, right? I get it, I get it.

7
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:27,400
Once you get it, shut up and follow me.

8
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:43,600
The teacher is a crazy old man.

9
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:47,820
Ningyo-yaki?

10
00:01:48,540 --> 00:01:50,820
That's right, the section
chief at the station asked me to.

11
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:53,400
Deliver 15 servings to Katsushika station.

12
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:57,180
Why do I have to do
such a troublesome thing?

13
00:01:57,620 --> 00:02:01,480
Ryo-chan's from Asakusa,
so he knows the good shops, right?

14
00:02:01,940 --> 00:02:02,840
That's right.

15
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:06,640
The recipients will be happy to get them from a famous shop,
you know.

16
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:11,300
You two aren't trying to leave all the troublesome stuff to me,
are you?

17
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:14,400
Stop whining and just go buy them.

18
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:17,880
Look, there should be
around 2,000 yen in change.

19
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:19,740
That's your tip.

20
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:20,920
Really?

21
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:23,900
I'm off, then.

22
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:28,100
Once Ryo-chan hears he gets a tip,

23
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:29,840
he really perks up, doesn't he?

24
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:33,100
It's a good deal for him, after all.

25
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:38,100
It's a regular shop, after all.

26
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:40,140
I got them to knock it
down to practically free!

27
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:43,000
An unexpected windfall!

28
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,020
Only the chief doesn't know.

29
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:47,020
And the ningyo-yaki are
fresh off the griddle, too.

30
00:02:47,020 --> 00:02:47,960
They look delicious.

31
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:51,020
There's this many in here!

32
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:52,700
Even if I take one or two,
nobody will notice.

33
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:55,260
Yum!

34
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:56,500
One more.

35
00:02:56,920 --> 00:02:58,080
That's not Kankichi.

36
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,780
What's the big idea, all of a sudden?

37
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:05,680
It's me, it's me.

38
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:08,840
Kankichi, don't you remember my face?

39
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:10,900
From when you were in elementary school.

40
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:14,520
That's right, from elementary school.
I was your homeroom teacher, Omagari.

41
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:17,480
Wow, it's been so long, hasn't it? Decades?

42
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:20,620
Teacher, you're still alive...
and still this healthy?

43
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:23,420
Of course. I'm as hale and hearty as ever.

44
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:27,700
Hale and hearty? Weren't you already quite old back then,
Teacher?

45
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:30,060
I'll be 90 this year.

46
00:03:30,060 --> 00:03:30,520
90?

47
00:03:32,660 --> 00:03:34,900
At seventy or eighty,
you're left to fend for yourself.

48
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:37,940
I'm in the prime of my youth right now,
Kankichi!

49
00:03:37,940 --> 00:03:41,580
Just how long do you plan
to keep on being young?

50
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:43,520
Did you say something?

51
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,380
Nothing. I'm glad you're doing well.

52
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:47,800
Please stay healthy forever.

53
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:49,580
By the way, Kankichi.

54
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:52,100
What kind of work are you doing now?

55
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:54,740
What kind of work?
As you can see, I'm doing my job.

56
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:57,840
Hmm.

57
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:59,500
I see, I see.

58
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:04,160
Oh my, that rowdy kid who was always
breaking something in the classroom.

59
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:07,720
Put like that,
it does feel strange to me too.

60
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:10,220
So you became a stewardess?

61
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:13,560
Hey, stewardesses are men, you know.
I'm a man!

62
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:15,440
Do you still have everything down there?

63
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:16,560
Of course I do.

64
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:17,900
Show me.

65
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:19,740
How could I show you here?

66
00:04:19,740 --> 00:04:21,440
I can show mine.

67
00:04:22,980 --> 00:04:24,260
Proof of manhood, that is.

68
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:36,820
Got teased by a 90-year-old.

69
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:41,520
No matter how old they get,
bad students stay bad students.

70
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:46,740
Sensei,
why were you walking around Nakamise?

71
00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:48,980
Just wandering about while out for a stroll.

72
00:04:48,980 --> 00:04:51,740
I live in an apartment
on Imakuko Street now.

73
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:54,320
You live in an apartment at your age?

74
00:04:54,980 --> 00:04:58,600
Chatting standing here isn't proper.
Let's talk over at that shop.

75
00:04:58,600 --> 00:04:59,880
Eel?

76
00:05:00,380 --> 00:05:03,060
Don't worry, it's my regular place.

77
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,300
Looks delicious.

78
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:12,080
Well, having a former
student is a real asset.

79
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:14,540
Getting treated to something this expensive

80
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:17,340
I never said I'd treat you.

81
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:18,820
What was that?

82
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:21,620
Besides,
I don't have enough money to treat anyone.

83
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:22,780
I can't hear you very well.

84
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:25,460
Once you get old,
your ears just get so hard of hearing.

85
00:05:25,460 --> 00:05:27,480
I don't have enough money to treat anyone.

86
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:28,320
What did you say?

87
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:29,440
I see, I see.

88
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:31,860
Master, add two plain grilled eels.

89
00:05:31,860 --> 00:05:35,600
Well, for a former student of mine,
you're really generous.

90
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:37,720
That's not it! I don't have any money!

91
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,020
Something about an unexpected windfall...

92
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:43,260
Everyone knows except the chief, they say.

93
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:46,060
Damn, you were listening?

94
00:05:46,060 --> 00:05:48,080
Nyahaha, shall we eat?

95
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:50,060
Yes, yes, owner, beer!

96
00:05:50,060 --> 00:05:52,860
Come on, Teacher,
you're getting carried away!

97
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:56,400
What? Sake too?
Owner, two more bottles of sake!

98
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:57,760
Ugh, here we go again.

99
00:05:57,760 --> 00:05:59,780
Put that on the teacher's tab.

100
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:00,911
Owner,

101
00:06:00,961 --> 00:06:04,360
After being a teacher for so long,
you get all sorts of students, you know.

102
00:06:05,820 --> 00:06:09,240
Setting the clock forward
an hour to end class early,

103
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:12,340
swiping lunch from the next class,

104
00:06:12,340 --> 00:06:16,440
or breaking a pricey cup in the principal's
office while trying to drink water from it.

105
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:20,700
Well, I always covered for you and kept it quiet,
so it all worked out.

106
00:06:20,700 --> 00:06:23,080
Who would've thought that
kid would become a cop?

107
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:24,540
Let's drink, Teacher!

108
00:06:24,540 --> 00:06:26,140
Today's on me.

109
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:27,860
How nostalgic.

110
00:06:27,860 --> 00:06:29,000
I see, I see.

111
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,440
Well, the kids like that are the ones who,

112
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:33,420
even as adults,
never forget the kindness of the past.

113
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:34,320
Splendid, splendid.

114
00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:36,980
Please order something expensive.

115
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:38,380
Damn, I lost.

116
00:06:39,520 --> 00:06:39,880
Thank you very much.

117
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:42,680
That was good, wasn't it.

118
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:45,440
Damn, the money I lent is totally wasted.

119
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:47,440
Well then, Teacher, I'll be going now.

120
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:49,060
Don't say such cold things.

121
00:06:49,060 --> 00:06:51,340
After all,
we've finally met again after thirty years.

122
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:52,620
A teacher and a student have reunited.

123
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:55,400
Something like this doesn't happen very often,
you know.

124
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:57,460
But I was asked by the Chief
to do this.

125
00:06:57,460 --> 00:07:00,000
I have to deliver these ningyo-yaki.

126
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,840
Ningyo-yaki

127
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:02,860
They look delicious.

128
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:04,480
No way, these are not for you.

129
00:07:05,820 --> 00:07:07,760
Kankichi was bad at arithmetic, wasn't he.

130
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:09,880
Well, have you gotten any better at it?

131
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:11,700
W-what's this all of a sudden?

132
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:14,760
Question one. There are 15 children here.

133
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:18,460
We need enough sweets to go
around for all of those children.

134
00:07:18,460 --> 00:07:20,120
How many would be enough?

135
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:22,420
Obviously 15, that's a given.

136
00:07:22,420 --> 00:07:25,840
You've gotten better at calculating,
haven't you?

137
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:28,700
So, how many people are you
giving those ningyo-yaki to?

138
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:30,860
Didn't you say they were for 15 people?

139
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:34,000
Then 15 would be enough, wouldn't it?

140
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,380
N-no, that won't do!

141
00:07:35,820 --> 00:07:38,440
One box is one serving,
and it holds eight pieces, you know.

142
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:42,360
Kankichi, what about the
ones you were eating just now?

143
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:46,720
No, that was just cutting
a serving down a little.

144
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:50,380
Right? If one serving is six pieces,
then you'd have two left over each time.

145
00:07:50,380 --> 00:07:52,840
Two times fifteen,
that's 30 pieces left over!

146
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:54,620
You're better at this than I am.

147
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:58,120
That's why I'm taking one bag from this lot.

148
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:01,880
The ningyo-yaki here really are the best.

149
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:03,040
Thank you, thank you.

150
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:06,100
A good former student is a treasure to have,
isn't he?

151
00:08:06,780 --> 00:08:08,840
I've been completely played.

152
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:15,740
I had a great time today, Kankichi.
Let's meet again.

153
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:16,820
See you.

154
00:08:18,820 --> 00:08:20,580
What an unlucky day that was.

155
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:25,140
That face...

156
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:26,380
Yo!

157
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:29,360
You're Tonpee, aren't you?

158
00:08:30,020 --> 00:08:31,000
Yes, that's right.

159
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,500
I'm Omagari, your homeroom
teacher from elementary school.

160
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:35,400
It's been a long time.

161
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,380
Teacher Omagari.

162
00:08:37,380 --> 00:08:39,320
What a coincidence.

163
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:41,060
So this is your shop?

164
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:42,400
Yeah, more or less.

165
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:44,580
You've grown into quite a fine man.

166
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:46,600
I'm so happy.

167
00:08:47,660 --> 00:08:50,660
Let's sit down and have
a long catch-up talk.

168
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:51,120
Okay?

169
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,960
Well then, you two too,

170
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:59,640
I was treated to sukiyaki.

171
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,350
the premium sushi and a rare,
hard-to-get fine sake,

172
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:06,100
got a whole bottle opened for free.

173
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:08,740
I got taken for eel and ningyo-yaki too.

174
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:11,580
I got chewed out by the Chief, honestly.

175
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:14,980
Even stingy Kankichi fell for it

176
00:09:15,620 --> 00:09:19,240
The teacher taught at an elementary
school in Asakusa for 40 years.

177
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:22,560
There are about 2,000 of his students in this neighborhood,
you know.

178
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:24,868
Ever since his wife passed away,

179
00:09:24,918 --> 00:09:27,780
When I can't be bothered to cook for myself,
I go out

180
00:09:27,780 --> 00:09:31,720
So you go around calling out to every
former student and pissing them off, huh

181
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:32,840
Damn, I got screwed over

182
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:36,300
But you really remember the faces of 2,000 people,
don't you

183
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:38,900
That's a memory you wouldn't
expect from a man in his nineties

184
00:09:38,900 --> 00:09:41,060
From now on, I'll just pretend
I don't know you when we meet

185
00:09:41,060 --> 00:09:44,660
That's the way to do it.
Once they get you on their pace, you've lost

186
00:09:44,660 --> 00:09:47,100
Truly a terrifying ninety-year-old

187
00:09:47,100 --> 00:09:48,120
Welcome!

188
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:49,940
Hello

189
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:52,140
It's Mugiki. Come on in

190
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:53,000
Hello

191
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:54,580
A foreigner

192
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:56,700
It's Tachibana's missus

193
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:01,020
He got married the other day.

194
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:03,140
So where did they meet, anyway?

195
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:06,300
Actually, it was at the
Asakusa Samba Carnival last year.

196
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:11,720
I was pulling the float she was riding on as a horse,
for a Junior Chamber job.

197
00:10:12,140 --> 00:10:15,960
Wow, the heir of Gofukuya marrying a foreigner's wife?
Who would have thought.

198
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:18,380
Asakusa really is becoming international,
isn't it.

199
00:10:19,940 --> 00:10:21,580
Well then, see you again sometime.

200
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:23,180
Anytime, just come by.

201
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:26,260
Tonpei, Chinkichi, let's go drinking soon!

202
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:31,200
Since you've come all this way,
why don't you stop in and take a look?

203
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:32,800
Look who it is!

204
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:37,260
That's dangerous! Darting out like that!

205
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:39,920
Well, what a coincidence!

206
00:10:39,920 --> 00:10:41,240
Omagari-sensei!

207
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:42,980
It's been a while.

208
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:45,180
We just saw each other the other day.

209
00:10:45,180 --> 00:10:49,040
Right, I'd like to have a
drink and talk over old times.

210
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:51,500
I won't fall for that trick again.

211
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:53,440
Now, where should we go?

212
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:55,980
No, no,
pretending you can't hear me won't work!

213
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:03,800
What's the matter all of a sudden?

214
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:07,360
Sensei.

215
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:09,740
Don't startle me like that.

216
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:10,860
What are you doing?

217
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:12,180
Nothing, really.

218
00:11:13,620 --> 00:11:14,740
Welcome!

219
00:11:14,740 --> 00:11:16,040
Mrs. Murasame.

220
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:19,320
Do you happen to have any nice obi clasps?

221
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:20,500
Obi clasps, you say?

222
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:21,680
Certainly, madam.

223
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:22,620
How beautiful.

224
00:11:22,620 --> 00:11:25,520
If you compare you to a flower,
you're a pristine white lily.

225
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,140
Eeeeeeeeh?!

226
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:29,660
Keep your voice down!

227
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:33,260
You're ninety!
Don't go falling in love at your age.

228
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:34,600
What are you talking about?

229
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:38,120
As Konosuke Matsushita,
the so-called god of management, once said,

230
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:40,680
"Youth is a state of mind."

231
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:41,960
Well then, Kankichi.

232
00:11:41,960 --> 00:11:43,920
Is that so?

233
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:46,380
So did you confess to her?

234
00:11:46,860 --> 00:11:49,220
Well, that's just... not yet.

235
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:51,400
Geez, that's not like you, Teacher.

236
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:54,360
What are you scared of?
It's just a date or two.

237
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:55,800
Well, you see...

238
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,960
Look, here she comes.
Quick, ask her out on a date!

239
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:02,440
N-no, n-no, n-no, n-not yet,
my heart's still sizzling!

240
00:12:02,460 --> 00:12:05,201
Come on, come on,
stop your fussing, a man needs guts.

241
00:12:05,251 --> 00:12:06,520
Just go for it, full force.

242
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:08,700
Whoaaaaa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

243
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:10,060
If it isn't Officer.

244
00:12:10,420 --> 00:12:12,970
Well, well, hello there.

245
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:15,100
What lovely weather we're having, isn't it.

246
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:17,000
Yes, it really is.

247
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:18,860
I wonder if it'll go well.

248
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:20,800
Well then.

249
00:12:21,260 --> 00:12:22,260
Take care.

250
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:25,200
Yes, thank you. Excuse me.

251
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:25,980
Thanks.

252
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:28,660
Sensei, how did it go?

253
00:12:28,660 --> 00:12:31,040
Did you get shot down?

254
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:37,620
It was a huge success!
I made a date with her!

255
00:12:37,620 --> 00:12:41,380
Don't scare me like that!
You did it, didn't you?

256
00:12:41,910 --> 00:12:43,920
But there's one problem.

257
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:45,300
A problem?

258
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:47,140
I've been lying.

259
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:52,660
When we met before, I told her I owned
three companies listed on the First Section.

260
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:55,140
What? Why would you tell such a lie?

261
00:12:57,240 --> 00:12:58,239
Please, Kankichi.

262
00:12:58,289 --> 00:13:01,700
If this gets out, Tokiko will hate me.

263
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:03,260
Do something about it, please.

264
00:13:03,460 --> 00:13:04,617
Even if you say "please"...

265
00:13:04,667 --> 00:13:07,620
You told me to ask her out too, didn't you?

266
00:13:07,780 --> 00:13:11,440
Hey, Kankichi, please.
Think of it as helping your former teacher.

267
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:13,180
Alright, alright.

268
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:15,680
Really? That's just like you, Kankichi.

269
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:18,660
We've really gotten
ourselves into a mess now.

270
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:33,860
Sorry to keep you waiting.

271
00:13:36,340 --> 00:13:38,780
The special-order limousine was too big,

272
00:13:38,780 --> 00:13:42,200
and there was no parking spot for it.
My apologies.

273
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:44,080
Pierre.

274
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:45,560
Me.

275
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:47,980
This is Pierre the sheep.

276
00:13:47,980 --> 00:13:51,000
If you need anything,
don't hesitate to tell me.

277
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:54,640
Pierre, say hello.

278
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:58,340
The sheep, no, no, it's Pierre the sheep.

279
00:13:58,540 --> 00:14:01,120
Please remember me, madam.

280
00:14:02,420 --> 00:14:03,760
What an interesting man.

281
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:07,200
I'm Murasame. The pleasure is mine.

282
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:09,340
Well then, shall we go?

283
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:12,755
Sitting like this,

284
00:14:12,805 --> 00:14:16,120
it brings back memories
of when I studied in Paris.

285
00:14:16,400 --> 00:14:18,860
I used to take walks along
the Seine all the time.

286
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:22,100
Paris? For art or something like that,
I suppose?

287
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:23,095
Yes, that's right.

288
00:14:23,145 --> 00:14:26,580
When I was young,
I meant to make my living as a painter,

289
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:27,835
but when my father passed away,

290
00:14:27,885 --> 00:14:31,000
I had no choice but to take
over the family business,

291
00:14:31,050 --> 00:14:32,940
so I came back to Japan.

292
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:35,740
If only I had stayed in Paris back then...

293
00:14:35,740 --> 00:14:39,900
you might have become a
world-famous painter by now.

294
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:42,653
But then, I wouldn't be here like this,

295
00:14:42,703 --> 00:14:46,320
and I never would have met
a beautiful woman like you.

296
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:49,840
That's just how fate works for people.

297
00:14:50,300 --> 00:14:53,940
Well, you certainly can reel
off one tall tale after another.

298
00:14:54,540 --> 00:14:58,160
Speaking of which, that reminds
me of the gondolas in Venice, too.

299
00:14:59,080 --> 00:15:00,703
Venice, the city of water,

300
00:15:00,753 --> 00:15:03,860
the days of my youth that will never return,

301
00:15:03,860 --> 00:15:05,261
how enviable,

302
00:15:05,311 --> 00:15:08,940
I've never even left Japan.

303
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:14,120
I imagine riding a gondola with
someone you love must be so romantic.

304
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:17,120
Well, of course,
that's right, this is Pierre!

305
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:19,632
Hey, Pierre! So that means me, then?

306
00:15:19,682 --> 00:15:22,640
Yes, what is it, master?

307
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:25,212
What are you doing with such a classic gag?

308
00:15:25,262 --> 00:15:26,960
Prepare a gondola.

309
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:28,120
A-a gondola?

310
00:15:28,740 --> 00:15:31,376
The Sumida River and Venice
are pretty much the same thing.

311
00:15:31,426 --> 00:15:33,480
Float a gondola right away.

312
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:35,440
Are they really the same?

313
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:38,140
You're dawdling! Get it ready right now.

314
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:41,000
Understood, master.
I'll get it ready right away.

315
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:43,974
Gondola, gondola,

316
00:15:44,024 --> 00:15:46,540
rocking on the waves, the gondola.

317
00:15:58,340 --> 00:15:59,920
Excuse me.

318
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:00,920
No.

319
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:01,700
Now then.

320
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:04,860
That shithead is going through hell, and yet

321
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:11,540
Here the river splits in two.

322
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:13,360
Over there is Harumigumo.

323
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:16,240
The bridge ahead is Chuo Bridge.

324
00:16:18,480 --> 00:16:20,280
Tohiko-san, look!

325
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:21,840
This is Kajidoki Bridge.

326
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:23,120
How nostalgic.

327
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:25,360
It's been ages since it last opened,
hasn't it?

328
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:28,200
Hey, this is Tokyo Bay.

329
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:35,820
It smells of the sea. That's the Rainbow Bridge.
I've never seen it before.

330
00:16:35,820 --> 00:16:45,500
Where are you going? You'll end up in the sea!
There it is, the TV station I bought last year.

331
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:51,340
Hey, it was a better bargain than I expected,
wasn't it, Pierre? Yes.

332
00:16:51,340 --> 00:16:56,760
Right, then next, shall we charter the Queen
Elizabeth for a Tokyo Bay cruise or something?

333
00:16:57,260 --> 00:17:01,760
Well, but more than that,
I'd like to go sightseeing in Tokyo.

334
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:05,160
Leisurely sightseeing in Tokyo, is it?
Understood.

335
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:08,740
Pierre,
bring the carriage around to the front.

336
00:17:08,740 --> 00:17:09,620
Carriage.

337
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:15,160
Lend me that float you used for the Samba Carnival,
why don't you?

338
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:17,180
You mean that float?

339
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:21,220
Yes, I believe the Junior Chamber
of Commerce prepared it, right?

340
00:17:21,220 --> 00:17:23,200
Where did they store it afterward?

341
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:25,640
Probably in the chamber's storehouse.

342
00:17:25,640 --> 00:17:27,220
Alright, take us there right away.

343
00:17:27,220 --> 00:17:28,360
The shop...

344
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:29,640
Leave it to me.

345
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:31,320
But that's...

346
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:32,860
It's fine, it's fine.

347
00:17:33,540 --> 00:17:36,320
Here we go! Hold on tight, everyone!

348
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:39,560
Count on you, Kankichi... I mean, Pierre!

349
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:40,080
There!

350
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:45,100
Clip-clop, clip-clop... No, Pierre!

351
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:46,240
Don't go so fast.

352
00:17:47,180 --> 00:17:47,940
You understand, right?!

353
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:49,840
Understood, sir!

354
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:51,580
Durred!

355
00:17:51,740 --> 00:17:55,340
This is the Kabuki-za. Let's come back
and see a kabuki show properly another time.

356
00:17:55,340 --> 00:17:55,800
Yes.

357
00:17:56,260 --> 00:17:59,920
At this speed,
we'll be out here until sundown!

358
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:01,740
This isn't a horse, it's a turtle.

359
00:18:03,300 --> 00:18:04,378
All day today,

360
00:18:04,428 --> 00:18:08,000
we've really had a wonderful time.

361
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:11,500
I'm glad you enjoyed it. I'm happy too.

362
00:18:12,140 --> 00:18:14,100
We really had a lot of fun.

363
00:18:17,180 --> 00:18:18,320
T-t-Tokiko-san?

364
00:18:19,260 --> 00:18:19,660
Yes?

365
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:22,040
M-m-m-me, I...

366
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:24,443
Um, that

367
00:18:24,493 --> 00:18:26,500
What do you think of me...?

368
00:18:26,500 --> 00:18:30,340
I think Mr. Omagari is a very nice man.

369
00:18:30,340 --> 00:18:32,954
S-so, t-then, me and...

370
00:18:33,004 --> 00:18:36,380
Tokiko-san, me and, m-m-m-marriage...

371
00:18:36,380 --> 00:18:38,280
I'm afraid it's too late.

372
00:18:39,740 --> 00:18:41,240
At this age,

373
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:42,680
That's not true.

374
00:18:42,680 --> 00:18:48,120
At my age, falling in love is
like snow falling in midsummer.

375
00:18:48,120 --> 00:18:49,360
Snow?

376
00:18:50,580 --> 00:18:50,980
Yes.

377
00:18:51,640 --> 00:18:54,840
So if it snows, you'll accept my proposal?

378
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:57,040
Such a miracle...

379
00:18:57,040 --> 00:18:59,480
I'll make that miracle happen for you.

380
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:00,800
Pierre, this is for you.

381
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:01,420
Yes.

382
00:19:02,180 --> 00:19:05,660
Snow! Make it snow enough to bury this park.

383
00:19:05,660 --> 00:19:07,160
Yes, certainly.

384
00:19:08,380 --> 00:19:08,780
Snow?

385
00:19:10,300 --> 00:19:10,700
Snow?

386
00:19:10,700 --> 00:19:11,760
That's right, snow! Snow!

387
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:18,000
I need you to gather all the artificial snow
machines from your ski resort at Ueno Park.

388
00:19:18,480 --> 00:19:20,160
But, senpai...

389
00:19:20,600 --> 00:19:27,560
I'll explain later. The teacher is on the verge of either grabbing
the greatest happiness of his life or falling into the depths of misery.

390
00:19:27,560 --> 00:19:29,020
Please, somehow.

391
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:31,500
Understood, I'll try to arrange it.

392
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:32,880
It's urgent, please.

393
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:33,220
Yes.

394
00:19:34,620 --> 00:19:39,720
But I'm too good-natured. There's not a single yen in it,
so why do I have to go through all this trouble?

395
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:48,120
Hey, Tokiko-san, I'll perform a miracle for you. So, so, I...
Your feelings make me happy, but even you can't do something like that.

396
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:52,740
No, there's nothing I can't do.
After all, I... I...

397
00:19:56,040 --> 00:20:02,400
I don't measure a person's worth by money or social standing,
Tokiko-san.

398
00:20:04,540 --> 00:20:08,200
There are people we can
respect even without any of that.

399
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:13,840
There are people who are loved by others even when they have nothing,
aren't there?

400
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:16,360
I think those people are the best.

401
00:20:18,060 --> 00:20:19,200
I-I...

402
00:20:20,940 --> 00:20:23,640
Tokiko-san, I-I'm sorry.

403
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:27,260
Omagari-san, w-what...?

404
00:20:27,260 --> 00:20:30,160
I-I've been lying to you.

405
00:20:30,940 --> 00:20:34,260
Saying I run several big
companies was a huge lie.

406
00:20:34,780 --> 00:20:36,780
I'm the worst man there is.

407
00:20:39,700 --> 00:20:41,500
Anyway, please stand up.

408
00:20:45,260 --> 00:20:49,040
I tried so hard to win your affection,

409
00:20:50,640 --> 00:20:55,380
but compared to your pure heart, I am such a

410
00:20:57,160 --> 00:21:00,000
contemptible man.

411
00:21:02,220 --> 00:21:04,240
Please, lift your face.

412
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:09,920
I knew it from the very beginning.

413
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:14,260
So you knew it was a lie
and still went along with me?

414
00:21:14,820 --> 00:21:15,660
I'm ashamed.

415
00:21:15,660 --> 00:21:18,880
And yet I piled lie upon lie.

416
00:21:19,860 --> 00:21:22,600
I am not worthy of you.

417
00:21:22,600 --> 00:21:24,380
I'm sorry for the trouble I've caused.

418
00:21:27,100 --> 00:21:29,920
Wait, Omagari-san, please. I...

419
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:31,980
Sensei sir...

420
00:21:31,980 --> 00:21:34,340
Kankichi, that's enough now.

421
00:21:34,340 --> 00:21:36,820
I've troubled you today, too.

422
00:21:36,820 --> 00:21:40,660
S-sensei, come now,
please hang in there a little longer.

423
00:21:42,220 --> 00:21:47,060
I was a student at the elementary school where Omagari-sensei taught.
My name is Ryotsu.

424
00:21:47,060 --> 00:21:50,040
So you were a schoolteacher?

425
00:21:50,040 --> 00:21:53,840
But now I'm just mooching
off those former students.

426
00:21:55,380 --> 00:22:02,680
You're a man! You're not acting like your usual self, sensei.
Have more confidence, Akichi... Okita-sensei.

427
00:22:03,180 --> 00:22:03,980
You.

428
00:22:03,980 --> 00:22:07,620
Everyone.

429
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:20,420
These people here are all your former students, Sensei.
They're the folks from this neighborhood who've all been mooched off by Omagari-sensei.

430
00:22:21,720 --> 00:22:22,740
Shushuman.

431
00:22:22,740 --> 00:22:25,560
Though everyone gets
to see you now and then,

432
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:27,880
they all look forward to
eating a meal together.

433
00:22:29,420 --> 00:22:33,040
That means you're loved by
this many people, Sensei.

434
00:22:33,040 --> 00:22:34,460
How wonderful.

435
00:22:34,460 --> 00:22:35,960
Oh my.

436
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:40,740
That's right, a miracle has happened.

437
00:22:41,320 --> 00:22:44,040
Kankishin, did you do this?

438
00:22:44,040 --> 00:22:45,500
It's a miracle, Sensei.

439
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:47,720
Sensei, a miracle is going to happen.

440
00:22:47,720 --> 00:22:49,660
Sensei, let's make a miracle happen too.

441
00:22:50,420 --> 00:22:51,300
For me...

442
00:22:51,700 --> 00:22:52,640
Omagari-san.

443
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:55,840
I was about to say something earlier, but...

444
00:22:56,400 --> 00:23:02,060
I was touched that you were willing
to lie and do something for me.

445
00:23:02,740 --> 00:23:06,560
Tokiko-san, th-then, will you forgive me?
This old fool?

446
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:11,220
Yes, if an old lady like me is fine,
let's go out together.

447
00:23:11,840 --> 00:23:13,220
T-Tokiko-san!

448
00:23:13,780 --> 00:23:14,440
Banzai!

449
00:23:15,540 --> 00:23:16,340
Banzai!

450
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:17,800
Banzai!

451
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:19,000
Banzai!

452
00:23:29,840 --> 00:23:31,520
Did we make it snow a little too much?

453
00:23:36,540 --> 00:23:38,200
Idiot!

454
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:40,820
Over there,
the snow still hasn't been cleared today,

455
00:23:40,820 --> 00:23:42,800
and traffic is in total chaos!

456
00:23:42,800 --> 00:23:44,000
With this heat,

457
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:45,980
it'll melt quickly if we leave it alone.

458
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:47,360
Idiot!

459
00:23:49,060 --> 00:23:49,440
What?

460
00:23:50,420 --> 00:23:50,640
Look!

461
00:23:51,540 --> 00:23:52,200
What is it?

462
00:23:52,680 --> 00:23:55,560
Go and clear all that snow away with this!

463
00:23:55,560 --> 00:23:59,460
Hey, don't you dare come
back until it's all cleared!

464
00:24:00,020 --> 00:24:01,940
There's no way I can do it alone!

465
00:24:04,900 --> 00:24:06,640
Welcome!

466
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:09,300
Welcome!

467
00:24:09,760 --> 00:24:11,380
Welcome! Please, come in.

468
00:24:12,240 --> 00:24:14,080
Welcome!

469
00:24:14,580 --> 00:24:16,280
Welcome! Please, come in.

470
00:24:17,060 --> 00:24:18,860
Welcome!

471
00:24:19,280 --> 00:24:20,960
Welcome!

472
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:23,920
Um, and, and and, hey

473
00:24:26,560 --> 00:24:28,320
Anago roll, jaga roll, salad roll

474
00:24:28,320 --> 00:24:30,280
Anything roll, roll... what should I get?

475
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:31,680
That's right!

476
00:24:32,360 --> 00:24:34,240
Do you have California rolls?

477
00:24:34,240 --> 00:24:36,300
We don't have California rolls.

478
00:24:37,240 --> 00:24:39,000
This isn't America, you know.

479
00:24:39,640 --> 00:24:40,520
Sorry, sori

480
00:24:41,560 --> 00:24:44,480
Uh, excuse me.

481
00:24:45,500 --> 00:24:46,280
Yes, mashamuse

482
00:24:47,580 --> 00:24:49,820
Then, kushiage, kakiage, katsuage.

483
00:24:49,820 --> 00:24:51,680
Fried-everything, fried-everything...
what was it?

484
00:24:52,300 --> 00:24:53,640
What do you recommend?

485
00:24:53,640 --> 00:24:56,960
Just watch out for katsuage.

486
00:24:56,960 --> 00:25:00,660
Was that a dad joke?

487
00:25:00,660 --> 00:25:02,260
Yes, sorry.

488
00:25:02,260 --> 00:25:04,760
I don't get it.

489
00:25:04,760 --> 00:25:08,220
Huh huh

490
00:25:08,220 --> 00:25:09,160
Seriously.

491
00:25:09,160 --> 00:25:11,080
Welcome!

492
00:25:11,080 --> 00:25:13,200
Welcome! Please, come in.

493
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:15,820
Welcome!

494
00:25:15,820 --> 00:25:18,020
Welcome! Please, come in.

495
00:25:18,020 --> 00:25:20,520
Welcome!

496
00:25:20,520 --> 00:25:22,700
Welcome! Please, come in.

497
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:27,200
Welcome!

498
00:25:30,200 --> 00:25:31,320
Where am I?

499
00:25:31,320 --> 00:25:33,380
What am I doing here?

500
00:25:33,380 --> 00:25:35,440
Wait, who the hell am I, anyway?

501
00:25:36,700 --> 00:25:38,240
I can't remember a thing.

502
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:39,420
By the way, I'm...

503
00:25:39,420 --> 00:25:41,980
Why do I keep calling myself "I"?

504
00:25:41,980 --> 00:25:44,040
Somebody tell me!

505
00:25:44,460 --> 00:25:46,540
Who am I next time?

506
00:25:47,020 --> 00:25:47,580
Nice to meet you.

507
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:59,260
Everyone, come on over to our town!

508
00:26:00,180 --> 00:26:00,860
Thank you!

